      "writtenOn": "2023-08-29T04:43:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks really strange that you\u0027d want a context aware service but not pass the context to the manager constructor. This method will cache the manager per-context ; you may or may not want that. The real question is : will the behavior be different depending on the context ? For networking usually it isn\u0027t, but maybe your case is different – you might want to behave differently when the context is for a docked state or something.\n\n- Do you intend to pass it eventually ? If so, I suggest you pass it immediately even if it\u0027s just to store it in a unused member. \n- Or, if you know the behavior doesn\u0027t depend on the context, then use registerStaticService.\n\nIf you don\u0027t know, it is generally prudent to pass a context.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 95,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 95,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "d3263bab403ef2a296ce870d6535fc6765480a77",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
